    "body": "## Problem\n\nDescribe the problem (concisely).\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\nlocal api = vim.api\n\nvim.ui.select = function()\n  local buf = api.nvim_create_buf(false, true)\n  api.nvim_open_win(buf, true, {\n    row = 10,\n    col = 10,\n    height = 10,\n    width = 10,\n    relative = \"editor\",\n    style = \"minimal\",\n  })\nend\n\nfor _ = 1, 49 do\n  api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, 0, false, { \"Praesent enim diam,\" })\nend\napi.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, -2, -1, false, { \"Praesent enim diam,\" })\n\napi.nvim_input(\"wz=\")\n```\n`E315: ml_get: Invalid lnum: 50`\n\n## Expected behavior\nNo errmsg.\n\n## System info\n\n- Nvim version (nvim -v): `v0.13.0-dev-1320 g1c9002a70e` neovim/neovim@1c9002a70e\n- Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?: ?\n- Operating system/version: Linux 7.1.8-zen1-3-zen\n- Terminal name/version: kitty\n- $TERM environment variable: `xterm-kitty`\n- Installation: ?\n\n",
